<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60559" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῡδρός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">,
			ʽκῦδοσ̓</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυδάλιμος</span>
			, in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always in fem., as epith. of Hera and Leto, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διὸς κυδρὴ παράκοιτις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					18.184
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.580
			</span></i>; of Pallas, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Hom.</u>
				28.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δίκη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					257
				</span></i>
			 (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυδνή</span>
			)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; θεαί</span>, of the Nymphs, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				168
			</span></i> (hex.); rarely of a mortal woman, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				15.26
			</span></i>: masc. first in <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Merc.</u>
				461
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alcm.
				9
			</span></i>; of a man, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Ap.</u>
				29
			</span></i>; of a horse, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυδρῷ τῷ σχήματι φέρεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					10.16
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυδρότερον πίνειν</span> to drink
				<i>more lustily</i>, Ion Eleg.<i><span class="en">
				2.10
			</span></i>.—Poet. word, used once in Trag., and twice by <i><span class="en">
				X.
			</span></i>—Besides regul. 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυδρότερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Xenoph.
					2.6
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				B.
				1.54
			</span></i>, we find <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυδίων, -ιστος</span> (v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύδιστος</span>), also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυδέστερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					3.96.7
				</span></i>
			: 
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυδίστατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυδότερος, -ότατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>EM</u>
					543.29
				</span></i>
			.</div>
